# macOS / cloud-sync duplicates. When a sync client sees the same file written
# twice it keeps both, naming the second one "page 2.html". These are never real
# files: they are stale copies of a page the build regenerates anyway, and
# committing one publishes an outdated duplicate of a live page at a second URL,
# which is an SEO problem as well as a mess.
#
# This rule exists because roughly 200 of them accumulated in one working session.
* [0-9].*
*\ [0-9].*
# Some sync clients use a parenthesised suffix instead: "page (1).html".
*\ \([0-9]\).*
# And some drop the extension entirely: "page 2" with no dot.
*\ [0-9]
*\ \([0-9]\)

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Local scratch that must never reach the public site
FETCH_HEAD
.wrangler/

# Build state, not a published artifact. generate-fund-pages.py reads this from
# the BUILD repo to put posts in the sitemap; the public site never needs it.
# The publish step deliberately copies only blog/*.html and blog/cards/*.png, so
# committing this here would just make it churn: added by hand, deleted by the
# next build, over and over.
blog/posts.json

# Working screenshots and scratch files left at the repo root by browser tooling.
# 78 of these had accumulated untracked; a blanket "git add -A" would have
# published every one to the live site. Anchored to the root with a leading
# slash so a genuinely named asset in a subfolder is never caught, and checked
# against the tracked list first: apple-touch-icon.png, crowdfunding.png and
# og-card.png are the only real root PNGs and none match these patterns.
/page-*.png
/homepage-*.png
/returnkoto-*.png
/ucb-*.png
/_tmp_*
